  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "A QUADRATIC has an x² term, like y = x² − 5x + 6. Its graph is a U-shaped parabola. Solve x² − 5x + 6 = 0 by factorising: (x − 2)(x − 3) = 0, so x = 2 or x = 3."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "EXPONENTS: 2⁵ = 32. Rules: aᵐ × aⁿ = aᵐ⁺ⁿ, and (aᵐ)ⁿ = aᵐⁿ."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "body": "A LOGARITHM asks 'what power?': log₂(32) = 5 because 2⁵ = 32. Logs turn multiplication into addition and appear in sound (decibels), earthquakes and pH."
    }
  ],
  "quiz": [
    {
      "q": "Solve x² − 7x + 12 = 0.",
      "options": [
        "x = 3 or x = 4",
        "x = 7 or x = 12",
        "x = −3 or x = −4"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "hints": [
        "Find two numbers that multiply to 12 and add to 7.",
        "Factorise: (x − ?)(x − ?) = 0.",
        "x² − 5x + 6 = (x − 2)(x − 3), so x = 2 or 3. Use the same method."
      ],
      "explain": "(x − 3)(x − 4) = 0, so x = 3 or x = 4."
    },
    {
      "q": "What is log₁₀(1000)?",
      "options": [
        "3",
        "100",
        "10"
      ],
      "answer": 0,
      "hints": [
        "Ask: 10 to what power gives 1000?",
        "10¹ = 10, 10² = 100, 10³ = …",
        "log₂(8) = 3 because 2³ = 8."
      ],
      "explain": "10³ = 1000, so log₁₀(1000) = 3."
